            <h2>Route Overview: Washington to Philadelphia</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Washington to Philadelphia by train is a convenient and scenic way to connect the nation's capital with one of America's most historic cities. This route provides passengers with a relaxed alternative to driving or flying - especially popular for business travelers, students, history enthusiasts, and weekend trips. While not as fast as high-speed rail in Europe, the Acela Express offers America's fastest train service, reaching up to 150 mph, with comfortable seating, onboard amenities, and views of the Mid-Atlantic corridor.</p>
            <p>The route is served by Amtrak's Acela Express and Northeast Regional, offering multiple daily departures between Washington Union Station and Philadelphia William H. Gray III 30th Street Station. Compared to road travel on the congested I-95 corridor, taking the train helps you avoid highway traffic. It makes city-center-to-city-center travel easy, without worrying about parking or renting a car in downtown Philadelphia.</p>
