                    <h3>What This Means for Travelers </h3>
                    <p>Taking the train between Washington and Philadelphia gives you a short, productive travel experience. It's often faster than flying when factoring in airport time, and allows you to relax, use Wi-Fi, stretch your legs, and enjoy views of the Chesapeake Bay, Baltimore, and Delaware. Compared to road travel, the train avoids I-95 traffic and delivers you straight into Philadelphia's University City/Center City without needing a car.</p>
                    Key Points:
